## Docker

- Socket only (no TCP). Never expose Docker TCP.
- Compose stacks: `{{ irl_compose_base }}/{stack}/docker-compose.yml`
- Shared networks: irl-frontend, irl-backend, irl-monitoring

## ZFS

- Pool: `{{ irl_zfs_pool }}` at `{{ irl_zfs_mount }}`
- Sacred data in `{{ irl_zfs_mount }}/nfs-share/` -- NEVER modify
- Service datasets: backups, artifacts, logs, ollama-models, gitea-lfs
- Snapshots managed by sanoid. Weekly scrubs via cron.

## SSH

- Root login DISABLED. Use `{{ irl_admin_user }}` with sudo.
- Key-only auth. Password auth disabled.

## Network

- Tailscale mesh: hostname `{{ irl_tailscale_hostname }}`
- Caddy reverse proxy on Tailscale interface
- nftables firewall: default deny, allow SSH + Tailscale + HTTP/S

## Rules for Agents

1. Do NOT modify files managed by Ansible (marked "Managed by Ansible")
2. Do NOT touch sacred data in {{ irl_zfs_mount }}/nfs-share/
3. Do NOT expose Docker TCP or disable the firewall
4. Do NOT modify /etc/ssh/sshd_config or /etc/nftables.conf directly
5. All infrastructure changes go through Ansible playbooks on the laptop
